        "original_id": "0fedb5b5-0dba-5d4a-80a7-2176d5e53b03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcus Hearn, Tom Spilsbury, Peter Robinson\n- Organizations: American Radio Relay League\n- Publications: Doctor Who Magazine, National Contest Journal, Birthright\n- Topics: magazine editors, publication frequency, prelude publication\n\nFacts:\n- The National Contest Journal, also called NCJ, is a bimonthly magazine published by the American Radio Relay League and has an independent volunteer editor.\n- In Doctor Who Magazine issue #203, author Peter Robinson published a prelude to the novel Birthright.\n- In July 2017, Marcus Hearn became the editor of Doctor Who Magazine, succeeding Tom Spilsbury.\n- Tom Spilsbury was the longest-serving editor of Doctor Who Magazine.",
